# Vercel AI + OpenAI (flashcard generation)

This app uses the **[Vercel AI SDK](https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs)** (`ai` on npm) to call **OpenAI** for AI features, especially **AI flashcard generation**.

## Product and access

- Gate routes, server actions, and UI on Clerk **`ai_flashcard_generation`** (see [clerk-billing.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/clerk-billing.mdc)); enforce the same checks server-side—never only on the client.
- Keep AI calls on the **server** (Server Actions or Route Handlers), validate inputs with **Zod**, and persist cards via Drizzle query helpers per [server-components-server-actions-zod.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/server-components-server-actions-zod.mdc) and [drizzle-db-access.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/drizzle-db-access.mdc).

## Structured output: array of N cards (`front` / `back`)

Use **`generateText`** with **`Output.object`** and a Zod schema whose **`cards`** array uses **`.length(cardCount)`** so the model must return exactly that many items. Build the schema when `cardCount` is known at runtime (do not hard-code the length in a static schema unless it is fixed).

```typescript
import { generateText, Output } from "ai";
import { z } from "zod";

const cardCount = 10;

const flashcardsOutputSchema = z.object({
  cards: z
    .array(
      z.object({
        front: z.string(),
        back: z.string(),
      }),
    )
    .length(cardCount),
});

const { output } = await generateText({
  model: "openai/gpt-5.3-chat",
  output: Output.object({
    schema: flashcardsOutputSchema,
  }),
  prompt: `Generate exactly ${cardCount} flashcards for the following topic or source material. Each card must have a concise front (question or prompt) and a clear back (answer). ...`,
});

// output.cards — { front: string; back: string }[], length === cardCount
```

Adjust the **`model`** string to match the project’s chosen OpenAI model id and any pinning in `package.json`. Keep prompts explicit about **exactly `cardCount` cards** to align with the schema.
